ion so if there is a  recession the trigger turns off but the  second part of that is if we do this  large tax cut and we broaden the base of  what's happening economically we better  not have a recession at that point this  should actually charge up the economy so  I think some of the concerns about a  pending recession right after you're  doing tax cuts are unfounded but we are  building language and to make sure that  we're protecting it either way because  obviously I don't want to have that  either  you'd want to have a situation where  you're in a recession in taxes go up and  we're not talking about a large tax  increase and we're talking about small  things around the edges to be able to  guard against if you  lost increases in deficits so that both  of those can be done well so senator let  me ask you a question about the  middle-class folks people making under  seventy five thousand dollars a year  would see a TAC heist attack tight in  2027  if these tax cuts aren't renewed  meanwhile the corporate tax cut is  permanent so why not make the tax cuts  for middle class individuals permanent  as well because of Washington scoring  that's why and that's been the  frustration all along that we have with  the Senate is the scoring requirements  running the bills that we do the way you  have to set it up it has to meet certain  standards in certain time periods we can  make all the business aspects permanent  which is very important to us you've got  to have some sort of consistency for  business to be able to plan for the  future for capital investment the  individual rates are not permanent but  that is exactly like what was done in  2001 and then never renewed in 2011 and  made permanent  I would assume we would have something  very similar to that with this one that  ten years out we would also renew those  and be able to keep going on it you need  to be able to protect rates you need to  be able to protect the economic growth  the way you do that is from the